  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to AICHR through HRWG</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Support to AICHR through HRWG</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to a coalition of Indonesian human rights civil society       organisations aiming at strengthening the ASEAN human rights          mechanism throught a proactive and constructive dialogue between the  civil society and ASEAN member states and ASEAN institutions, e.g.    AICHR.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Support to a coalition of Indonesian human rights civil society       organisations aiming at strengthening the ASEAN human rights          mechanism throught a proactive and constructive dialogue between the  civil society and ASEAN member states and ASEAN institutions, e.g.    AICHR.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project entitled &#x201c;Promoting Fundamental Freedoms by Ensuring an Effective, Accessible and Responsive ASEAN Human Rights System&#x201d; was designed to be a three-year project from 2011 to 2013. It was expected that by end of the project, ASEAN and its human rights mechanisms would be more accessible, responsive and effective.
There were three results to be achieved by implementing the project. They were:
1) ASEAN&#x2019;s procedures, mechanisms and standards to protect human rights are in line with /promote the international human rights principles and values.
2) A Strategic working relationship between civil society and ASEAN Human Rights Mechanisms that encourage dialogue and engagement.
3) Documentation and preservation of lessons learnt to be shared among civil society in engaging ASEAN human rights systems.</narrative>
  </description>
